Port of CrossOver's CW Hack 24834 to Wine 11.14: optionally force the
forward-compatible bit when creating an OpenGL 3.2+ context on macOS.

macOS grants OpenGL 3.2+ only through a forward-compatible core profile. A caller
that asks for 3.2+ without WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB is rejected, and
wined3d is one such caller -- so it silently falls back to a legacy 2.1 context,
capping D3D feature level at 9_x, capping ANGLE at GLES 2.0, which is why
Chromium-based apps (the Steam client) render a black window.

Gated behind WINEMAC_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX=1 so stock behaviour stays reachable for
A/B testing, and so it is inert unless explicitly requested.

PROVENANCE NOTE: this change was made in an earlier session and applied directly
to src/wine WITHOUT a patch file, so `bin/build-runtime` from a clean checkout
would silently have dropped it -- breaking the reproducibility guarantee that
docs/NOTEBOOK.md claims. Extracted here to close that hole.

STATUS: likely redundant once the tree is rebased onto CrossOver's Wine, which
carries CW Hack 24834 already. Kept so nothing is lost in the transition.

Source: CrossOver 26.0.0 (LGPL), dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index 6b2ec0bc..061331cf 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2134,6 +2134,28 @@ static BOOL macdrv_context_create(int format, void *share, const int *attrib_lis
     if ((major == 3 && (minor == 2 || minor == 3)) ||
         (major == 4 && (minor == 0 || minor == 1)))
     {
+        /* macOS grants OpenGL 3.2+ only through a forward-compatible core
+         * profile. Callers that ask for 3.2+ without the forward-compatible bit
+         * are rejected below -- and wined3d is one of them, so it silently falls
+         * back to a legacy 2.1 context. That caps D3D feature level at 9_x,
+         * which caps ANGLE at GLES 2.0, which is why Chromium-based apps (the
+         * Steam client) render a black window.
+         *
+         * Setting the bit on the caller's behalf can only improve matters: the
+         * alternative is outright failure. Gated by an env var so the stock
+         * behaviour stays reachable for A/B testing.
+         *
+         * Ported from CrossOver 26 (CodeWeavers "CW Hack 24834", LGPL). */
+        const char *force_fwd_compat = getenv("WINEMAC_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX");
+        if (force_fwd_compat && force_fwd_compat[0] == '1')
+        {
+            if (!(flags & WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB))
+            {
+                TRACE("forcing forward-compatible bit for %u.%u context\n", major, minor);
+                flags |= WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB;
+            }
+        }
+
         if (!(flags & WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB))
         {
             WARN("OS X only supports forward-compatible 3.2+ contexts\n");
